   "title": "Passive ～られる: was done (to me)",
   "explain": "U-verbs: u → a + れる (ふむ → ふまれる). Ru-verbs: られる (ほめる → ほめられる). The doer takes に. Japanese also uses it when something annoying happens to you: 足をふまれた (someone stepped on my foot).",
